From: rijads <spaha92@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 09:14:46 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Play with the controller alone on the PS5

Gamepad replaces GamepadPointer. The left stick moves the pointer with a curve, slower over
buttons and faster when held at full tilt; pushing it against the edge of the screen scrolls
the park. The d-pad moves the pointer from button to button across windows, row by row or cell
by cell through lists (WindowBase::onScrollGetItems, with grids for new rides and scenery and the
scenarios without their headings), along sliders, and through open dropdowns, which it enters
once Cross is let go. Circle goes back: closes a dropdown, an error, a text box, a tool and its
window, or the window under the pointer (or the frontmost one with a close button). L1 and R1
switch the tabs of the window under the pointer or rotate the view; R3 rotates, L3 pauses, L2
and R2 zoom towards the pointer. The right stick scrolls the list under the pointer, or the park.

While building track or a bridge path with the pointer over the park, the d-pad turns and
slopes the piece, Cross builds it (held, it keeps building), Square takes it away, L1 and R1
bank and Triangle toggles the chain lift; Triangle otherwise rotates the object being placed.
The controller rumbles lightly as the pointer jumps and when building.

The joystick shortcut bindings on the PS5 are gone: the controller is handled here.
